  node [
    id 57
    label "zlGdjdNgJv4"
    step 0
    date "2021-03-04T21:00:14Z"
    title "Tourettes Syndrome Under 6 Minutes"
    description "Tourette&#8217;s Syndrome is a neurodevelopmental disorder that affects&#13;nearly 4% of children, often manifesting between the ages of 6-8. The main characteristics of&#13;this disorder are the motor and vocal tics. Tics are sudden and rapid movements or vocalizations&#13;that are difficult to suppress. This video will present additional background information on&#13;Tourette&#8217;s, highlight the different presentations of motor and vocal tics, and outline steps&#13;individuals with Tourette&#8217;s can take in order to suppress sudden outbursts in their movement or&#13;speech.&#10;&#10;This video was made by McMaster students Armaan Sekhon, &#13;Kriti Manuja, &#13;Sharleen Maduranayagam and Krishna Patel in collaboration with the McMaster Demystifying Medicine Program.&#10;&#10;Copyright McMaster University 2021&#10;&#10;References:&#13;&#10;&#10;American Psychiatric Association. (2013). Diagnostic and statistical manual of mental disorders&#13;(5th ed.). https://doi.org/10.1176/appi.books.9780890425596&#13;CDC. (2018, October 29). &#10;&#10;Risk Factors and Causes for Tourette Syndrome | CDC . Centers for&#13;Disease Control and Prevention. https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/tourette/riskfactors.html&#13;&#10;&#10;Chao, T.-K., Hu, J., &#38; Pringsheim, T. (2014). Prenatal risk factors for Tourette Syndrome: A&#13;systematic review. BMC Pregnancy and Childbirth , 14 , 53.&#13;https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2393-14-53&#13;&#10;&#10;Cox, J. H., Nahar, A., Termine, C., Agosti, M., Balottin, U., Seri, S., &#38; Cavanna, A. E. (2019).&#13;Social stigma and self-perception in adolescents with tourette syndrome. Adolescent&#13;Health, Medicine and Therapeutics , 10 , 75&#8211;82. https://doi.org/10.2147/AHMT.S175765&#13;&#10;&#10;F&#233;lix, M.-A., &#38; Barkoulas, M. (2015). Pervasive robustness in biological systems. Nature&#13;Reviews Genetics , 16 (8), 483&#8211;496. https://doi.org/10.1038/nrg3949&#13;&#10;&#10;Gill, C. E., &#38; Kompoliti, K. (2020). Clinical Features of Tourette Syndrome. Journal of Child&#13;Neurology , 35 (2), 166&#8211;174. https://doi.org/10.1177/0883073819877335&#13;&#10;&#10;Krewski, D., Barakat-Haddad, C., Donnan, J., Martino, R., Pringsheim, T., Tremlett, H., van&#13;Lieshout, P., Walsh, S. J., Birkett, N. J., Gomes, J., Little, J., Bowen, S., Candundo, H.,&#13;Chao, T.-K., Collins, K., Crispo, J. A. G., Duggan, T., El Sherif, R., Farhat, N., &#8230;&#13;Cashman, N. R. (2017). Determinants of neurological disease: Synthesis of systematic&#13;reviews. Neurotoxicology , 61 , 266&#8211;289. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuro.2017.04.002"
