    step 0
    date "2021-03-08T18:05:11Z"
    title "Why students with Tourette Syndrome need an Occupational Therapist"
    description "While Tourette Syndrome is a neurological disorder, there are often co-occurring conditions that may be more troublesome than the actual tics. In this webinar, Occupational Therapists learn how to apply their expertise to assess underlying factors that are impeding progress and develop a team-oriented approach for success in school, home, and community. We also discuss the development of strengths, self-awareness, and advocacy skills needed for ongoing success.&#10;&#10;Please note: CE credits were only available for the live webinar."
