    title "Tourette Syndrome: Classroom Strategies"
    description "As a classroom teacher, what are ways you can best support a student with Tourette Syndrome? &#10;&#10;Tourette Syndrome is a neurodevelopmental disorder that becomes evident in early childhood or adolescence.  1 out of every 100 children has Tourette Syndrome or another Tic Disorder. People with Tourette Syndrome may experience one or more comorbid conditions such as ADHD, OCD, dysregulated behaviors, anxiety, sensory processing disorder, and more.&#10;&#10;Presenter Kathy Giordano is a mother, advocate, and nationally recognized Tourette expert. Join us as Kathy shares her wisdom and practical advice on ways you can understand Tourette Syndrome and support kids in your class."
