    label "PiOx01HQL9E"
    step 0
    date "2018-01-15T18:00:02Z"
    title "Kids With Tourettes Syndrome Talk About Experiences | Growing Up | Real Families"
    description "It is thought that one in 100 school children are affected by Tourette&#8217;s Syndrome, a neurological condition affecting the brain and nervous system that is characterised by involuntary, random sounds and movements, known as tics - most are boys.&#10;&#10;There is no cure, but there is hope, thanks to the pioneering treatment programme at the world renowned leading children&#8217;s hospital Great Ormond Street. This moving documentary follows the lives of three boys and their families over a six-month period as they share the reality of living with the condition and the daily obstacles they face. This is their story, in their own words.&#10;&#10;Real Families brings you stories of modern day family life from around the world through the eyes of children, parents, and parenting experts. &#10;Subscribe for weekly documentaries and full episodes of evergreen family documentaries and parenting TV shows. &#10; &#10;Subscribe for more from Real Families: https://goo.gl/y8WzCa&#10; &#10;Follow us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/RealFamilies/&#10; &#10;Check us out on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/realfamilieschannel/&#10; &#10;We&#8217;re on TikTok too: https://www.tiktok.com/@realfamilies&#10;&#10;Content Licensed by All3Media to Little Dot Studios &#10;&#10;Any queries, please contact us at: owned-enquiries@littledotstudios.com&#10;&#10;#RealFamilies #Documentary #Tourette"
