  node [
    id 170
    label "xgdyi_I79v4"
    step 0
    date "2013-12-19T22:50:22Z"
    title "What Makes Me Tic? Documentary Film, Tourettes Syndrome"
    description "Director/Producer:  Matt Duhamel: http://www.imdb.com/name/nm6055103/?ref_=tt_ov_dr&#10;Producer:  Heather Duhamel&#10;&#10;When we are faced with overwhelming challenges in our lives, it is often said that it's not the challenges themselves, but it's how we react to them that matters.  We may be surprised that sometimes the challenges we face can often motivate us to achieve more than we ever expected.  &#10;&#10;The documentary film, &#34;What Makes Me Tic?&#34; is a powerful look into four average Americans living with the often misunderstood disorder, Tourette's Syndrome.  How do their &#34;tics&#34; affect their daily lives?  Are they seen as weird or crazy in public?  Does living with Tourette's cause them to be anti-social or depressed?  These questions are answered when &#34;What Makes Me Tic?&#34; interviews Natasha, Josh, Calvert and Peter to find out how they live and work with the disorder.  &#10;&#10;Review the film at:  http://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/what_makes_me_tic/&#10;&#10;Buy the DVD with Bonus Features on Amazon:&#10;http://www.amazon.com/What-Makes-Tic-Matt-Duhamel/dp/B00HDU3WJQ/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&#38;qid=1387321947&#38;sr=8-1&#38;keywords=matt+duhamel&#10;&#10;For more information on this film and future releases, visit http://www.metamorafilms.org"
    channeltitle "Metamora Films"
