  node [
    id 240
    label "U8iO92tDX9w"
    step 0
    date "2022-05-02T09:20:10Z"
    title "Where Ellie Learned Cuss Words | Coprolalia  Tourette Syndrome"
    description "Besides actual Tourette syndrome questions, this is the question we get the most. Where did Ellie learn to cuss? Probably from us and then you know... that big crazy thing you also reside in called THE WORLD, LOL! If your kids haven't heard cuss words.. congrats to you, they will one day! Coprolalia is an aspect of Tourette syndrome that includes obscene words and gestures. Ellie is still literally THE NICEST human in the world but when she uses cuss words during tics, she make sound or appear aggressive when it couldn't be further from the truth. Did you know that using profanity can alleviate physical pain... and that there is a physical build up before a tic happens? It makes SO MUCH sense why 10% of people with Tourette syndrome have coprolalia when you look at it this way. When you watch our videos or hang out on our social media communities, you can't deny we that our kids are so well-loved and doing so much good in this world already. The fact that they've heard cuss words is just beyond insignificant. But, since you may have asked... we made this video for you.&#10;&#10;Sign up for the Tourette syndrome newsletter here and never miss out on content we share!: https://view.flodesk.com/pages/61a79b2aaadf79eb4003551f"
    channeltitle "Amanda Hedgepeth"
