    date "2020-06-02T14:00:14Z"
    title "Stuttering Q Managing Stuttering"
    description "Skip to the questions you want to hear!&#10;&#10;0:39 &#34;What tics do you have with your Tourette's? Can you show them happening?&#34;&#10;1:41 &#34;How does your Tourette's present itself day to day?&#34;&#10;2:35 &#34;Do your jerks have anything to do with stuttering? Are they medication induced or anxiety related?&#34;&#10;3:32 &#34;Are there certain letters that make you stutter depending on how they're pronounced?&#34;&#10;4:43 &#34;Would you speak to a waiter yourself or have someone do it for you?&#34;&#10;5:12 &#34;Is your stutter hereditary?&#34;&#10;5:37 &#34;What are some techniques to be more fluent and have confidence?&#34;&#10;8:01 &#34;Do you get annoyed when someone asks you about your stutter?&#34;&#10;9:15 &#34;Do you have a word that is really hard to say?&#34;&#10;10:14 &#34;What is your favorite book if you have one?&#34;&#10;11:06 &#34;Do you have any advice on how to convince my family that my stuttering isn't negative?&#34;&#10;&#10;Subscribe to stay updated with more related videos!&#10;Check out &#38; follow my Instagram! @stutteringslp"
