    label "b29Eicx5wow"
    step 0
    date "2021-08-06T17:44:20Z"
    title "Research into Tourette Syndrome!"
    description "We need young people aged 13-25 to take part in our online research into movement control in Tourette Syndrome! &#10;FREE GAME SHEET LINKED IN DESCRIPTION &#10;&#10;First, you&#8217;ll be asked to fill in some short questionnaires about your demographic info, handedness, impulsivity, cognitive skills, and your experience of tics. This will take around 15-20 minutes. This MUST be completed first! &#10;Go here to fill in the questionnaires: www.tinyurl.com/TSquestions &#10;&#10;Once you&#8217;ve done that, you can then start playing our games!&#10;You can play as many of our four online games as you&#8217;d like. These can each be played on separate days, it&#8217;s all up to you. You&#8217;ll have the opportunity to enter into separate prize draws to win an Amazon voucher with each game played. &#10;&#10;Here are the links to our four games:&#10;1. Task switching in TS: www.tinyurl.com/TSswitching &#10;2. Action-outcome prediction in TS: www.tinyurl.com/TSprediction&#10;3. Sensorimotor synchronisation in TS: www.tinyurl.com/TSsynch&#10;4.  Predictive motor timing in TS: www.tinyurl.com/TStiming&#10;&#10;Download a free game sheet here with the links to all of the games:&#10;https://drive.google.com/file/u/3/d/1qzKJ8JPwIeh3KnfnxwSEBhYLtPh7yf_g/view?usp=sharing&#10;&#10;Email hannah.slack@nottingham.ac.uk with any questions! &#10;&#10;Thank you for your support! Our research wouldn't be possible without you!&#10;Happy gaming! :)"
    channeltitle "HannahSlackResearch"
