  node [
    id 287
    label "8pyrs7JUdfc"
    step 0
    date "2022-03-29T12:47:25Z"
    title "Tourette Syndrome: How intense focus can distract from tics sometimes #tourettes #tourettesyndrome"
    description "Tourette&#8217;s people get asked, &#8220;Can&#8217;t you just stop ticcing?&#8221; The answer is no, we can&#8217;t just stop ticcing.  When the brain sends an electrical signal down a nerve, the muscle at the end of that nerve is going to twitch, whether we like it or not. But there are moments when we can distract our brain from ticcing by participating in certain activities that require intense focus.  It&#8217;s different for every person.  For me, things like juggling, BMX biking, playing music, and drawing, require enough focus that I don&#8217;t tic much, if at all while doing them.  There are even famous athletes, actors, and musicians with Tourette&#8217;s that you don&#8217;t even know about because their brains are able to keep it under control when focused on their special activities.  It&#8217;s nice to have a momentary break, which is why I love these activities so much. &#128578; #tourettes #tourettesyndrome #tourettesawareness #tourettesyndromeawareness #tourettetalent #tourettestalent #tic #tics #coprolalia #copropraxia #coprographia #coprophenomena #tourettewarrior #touretteswarrior #peoplewithtourettes #ticcing #juggling #juggle #jugglingvideos #slowmo #relaxing #jugglingexercise #ticrelief #relieffromtics"
    channeltitle "Tourettes Life / BMX / Animation / RC Trucks"
    channelid "UCHbBoaoqpTfsPk6EhDJMmoQ"
