  node [
    id 363
    label "tPXX1BJVYog"
    step 0
    date "2022-04-18T06:33:46Z"
    title "My Life With Tourette Syndrome/ The Funny But Important Experiences That Make Me, Me!"
    description "In 4th grade, I was diagnosed with Tourette Syndrome (TS) and ADHD and since then it has been a major variable in how I have become the person I am today. Many people know me for my political, and economic beliefs, but now I provide more insight into what it's like living with Tourettes. In this video, I share my personal experience as well as several stories that, while funny, played a very pivotal role in my journey to where I am at today! I have not done a great job in raising awareness for Tourette Syndrome, and I have never believed that I am a good spokesperson for the disorder. But I would like to bring awareness to the people that have it way worse than I do!&#10;&#10;Tourette Syndrome can have a major impact on a person's life and I have been blessed that I can view TS as a positive factor for myself. It makes me, me! Please feel free to ask questions and If you have Tourettes and you need advice or need someone to talk to, please feel free to reach out!&#10;#TouretteSyndrome #Tourettes #TS #Tics #Tourettesawareness #ADHD &#10;&#10;For more information on Tourette Syndrome visit:&#10;https://www.ninds.nih.gov/Disorders/Patient-Caregiver-Education/Fact-Sheets/Tourette-Syndrome-Fact-Sheet&#10;&#10;https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/tourette/facts.html"
    channeltitle "Real Conservative Talk"
    channelid "UC-rDUlcIAqI9qFaTPEFqTFQ"
